  "passage": "Ryan forgot his jacket on the coldest day of winter. He tried to act normal, but his hands were shaking.\nDuring lunch, a classmate named Owen gave him a jacket. Ryan was surprised because they were not close friends.\n\"Why\" Ryan asked.\nOwen said, \"Someone helped me last year when I forgot mine.\"\nRyan wore the jacket all afternoon. The next day, he returned it with a thank-you note.\nWeeks later, Ryan saw a younger student standing outside without a coat. He remembered Owen and offered his own jacket.\nThe jacket had not only kept him warm. It had also carried a simple message from one person to another: help does not have to stop with the person who receives it.",
